From 943d1dc2946fb5cf9d01032089e0476ce09339b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jewel Chowdhury <portgasdjewel@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:38:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] new feature: allow selecting text by dragging the mouse

When the mouse is enabled, pressing the first button in the edit window
and moving the pointer while the button is held selects the text between
the two spots, like a shifted selection.  While the pointer rests above
or below the edit window, the viewport keeps scrolling, so a selection
can be extended beyond what is visible.

Ncurses asks the terminal only for button events (xterm mode 1000), also
when REPORT_MOUSE_POSITION is in the mask, so nano asks for drag events
(mode 1002) itself -- again each time that ncurses has reinitialized the
mouse, after a resize or a suspension.  The click interval is set to zero
to get the raw presses and releases.

When several mouse events arrive together, ncurses reports them with one
KEY_MOUSE, after which getmouse() returns them one by one.  So, fetch all
of them, and handle them oldest first.  (Since its 20250913 patch, ncurses
returns such a run of events oldest first; before, newest first.)

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
